  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Turntable\n\nA product card with real thickness spins on an invisible turntable through front, edge and back, with face shading, a moving sheen and a floor shadow. The faces are placeholders; a host puts its own content in the .tt-front and .tt-back markup in the script.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A physical-looking object, such as a credit card, a membership pass or a ticket, should be shown from every side.\n- A product launch needs a hero beat where the object turns once and settles facing the camera.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The content is a long page or recording the camera should travel across: use stage.\n- A flat word should pop out of the plane into 3D: use extrude-pop.\n\nVariables:\n- thickness (number, 4-80): Thickness, default 22\n- turns (number, 0.25-4): Turns, default 1\n- tilt (number, -30-30): Tilt, default 8\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- front_color (color): Front, default \"#E5322D\"\n- back_color (color): Back, default \"#F2F2F2\"\n- edge_color (color): Edge, default \"#A3201C\"\n- mark_color (color): Mark, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- shadow_color (color): Shadow, default \"#000000\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Turntable\n\n  A product card with real thickness spins on an invisible turntable through front, edge and back, with face shading, a moving sheen and a floor shadow. The faces are placeholders; a host puts its own content in the .tt-front and .tt-back markup in the script.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/turntable/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"turntable\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"thickness\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Thickness\", \"description\": \"Card thickness in px at 720p.\", \"default\": 22, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 80, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"turns\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Turns\", \"description\": \"Full rotations per spin.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.25},\n    {\"id\": \"tilt\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Tilt\", \"description\": \"Camera tilt in degrees; positive looks down on the card.\", \"default\": 8, \"min\": -30, \"max\": 30, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"deg\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Stage background.\", \"default\": \"#111111\"},\n    {\"id\": \"front_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Front\", \"description\": \"Default front face color.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"},\n    {\"id\": \"back_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Back\", \"description\": \"Default back face color.\", \"default\": \"#F2F2F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"edge_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Edge\", \"description\": \"Card edge color.\", \"default\": \"#A3201C\"},\n    {\"id\": \"mark_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Mark\", \"description\": \"Color of the marks on the default front.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"shadow_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Shadow\", \"description\": \"Floor shadow color.\", \"default\": \"#000000\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Turntable</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 40% at 50% var(--floor), rgba(255,255,255,0.07), rgba(255,255,255,0) 70%), var(--background); }\n        .tt-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }\n        .tt-shadow { position: absolute; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--shadow); }\n        .tt-persp { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .tt-card { position: relative; transform-style: preserve-3d; }\n        .tt-face { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; backface-visibility: hidden; }\n        .tt-sheen, .tt-dark { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .tt-dark { background: #000; }\n        .tt-slab { position: absolute; background: var(--edge); }\n        /* Default faces. A host replaces the contents of .tt-front / .tt-back with its own markup. */\n        .tt-front { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: var(--front); padding: 9%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; }\n        .tt-ring { width: 22%; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; border: 0.6em solid var(--mark); }\n        .tt-lines { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5em; }\n        .tt-line { height: 0.9em; background: var(--mark); border-radius: 99px; }\n        .tt-backf { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: var(--back); }\n        .tt-strip { position: absolute; top: 16%; left: 0; right: 0; height: 18%; background: #111111; }\n        .tt-chip { position: absolute; right: 9%; bottom: 12%; width: 16%; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 28%; background: var(--front); }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"turntable\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"tt-clip\" class=\"tt-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div class=\"tt-shadow\" id=\"tt-shadow\"></div>\n          <div class=\"tt-persp\" id=\"tt-persp\">\n            <div class=\"tt-card\" id=\"tt-card\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"turntable\";\n\nvar root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\nvar vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\nfunction num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\nfunction str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\nfunction col(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && /^#([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.test(v.trim()) ? v.trim() : f; }\nfunction bool(v, f) { return v === true || v === \"true\" ? true : v === false || v === \"false\" ? false : f; }\nvar FPS = 30;\nvar DUR = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\nvar TOTAL = Math.round(DUR * FPS);\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\nfunction cl(x, a, b) { return Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)); }\n// interpolate(x, [in...], [out...], easing): clamped on both sides, easing applied per segment.\nfunction interp(x, inp, out, easing) {\n  if (x <= inp[0]) return out[0];\n  if (x >= inp[inp.length - 1]) return out[out.length - 1];\n  var i = 0;\n  while (x > inp[i + 1]) i++;\n  var t = (x - inp[i]) / (inp[i + 1] - inp[i]);\n  if (easing) t = easing(t);\n  return out[i] + (out[i + 1] - out[i]) * t;\n}\nfunction bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n  return function (x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0; if (x >= 1) return 1;\n    var t = x;\n    for (var i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n      var cx = 3 * x1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * x2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t - x;\n      var d = 3 * x1 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) - 6 * x1 * t * (1 - t) + 6 * x2 * t * (1 - t) - 3 * x2 * t * t + 3 * t * t;\n      if (Math.abs(cx) < 1e-6 || Math.abs(d) < 1e-6) break;\n      t -= cx / d;\n    }\n    t = cl(t, 0, 1);\n    return 3 * y1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * y2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t;\n  };\n}\nvar E = {\n  lin: function (t) { return t; },\n  quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n  cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n  sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); }\n};\nfunction eOut(f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; }\nfunction eInOut(f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(2 * t) / 2 : 1 - f(2 - 2 * t) / 2; }; }\nvar outCubic = eOut(E.cubic), outQuad = eOut(E.quad), inCubic = E.cubic, inQuad = E.quad;\nvar inOutCubic = eInOut(E.cubic), inOutQuad = eInOut(E.quad), inOutSin = eInOut(E.sin), outSin = eOut(E.sin);\n// Damped spring from 0 to 1 (rest at 1, no initial velocity), frames at 30 fps.\nfunction spring(frame, cfg) {\n  if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n  var m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n  var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m)), t = frame / FPS;\n  if (z < 1) {\n    var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n    return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n  }\n  if (z === 1) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n  var s = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + s, r2 = -z * w0 - s;\n  return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n}\n// Seeded random: same string in, same number out.\nfunction rnd(seed) {\n  var sd = String(seed), h = 1779033703 ^ sd.length;\n  for (var i = 0; i < sd.length; i++) { h = Math.imul(h ^ sd.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353); h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19); }\n  h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507); h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909); h ^= h >>> 16;\n  var a = (h >>> 0);\n  a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n  t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n  return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n}\nfunction rgb(h) {\n  h = h.replace(\"#\", \"\");\n  if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n  return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];\n}\nfunction mixc(a, b, t) {\n  var x = rgb(a), y = rgb(b);\n  return \"rgb(\" + Math.round(lerp(x[0], y[0], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[1], y[1], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[2], y[2], t)) + \")\";\n}\nfunction rgba(h, a) { var x = rgb(h); return \"rgba(\" + x[0] + \",\" + x[1] + \",\" + x[2] + \",\" + a + \")\"; }\nvar SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\nfunction svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n  var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n  for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n  if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n  return e;\n}\nfunction setA(e, attrs) { for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); }\n// Drive draw(frame) from the timeline; frames run 0..frames over frames/30 seconds.\nfunction drive(draw, frames) {\n  var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n  var clock = { frame: 0 };\n  tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n  draw(0);\n  return tl;\n}\nfunction finish(tl) {\n  if (tl.duration() < DUR) tl.to({}, { duration: DUR - tl.duration() });\n  tl.seek(0);\n  window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n  window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n}\n\n\nvar persp = document.getElementById(\"tt-persp\"), card = document.getElementById(\"tt-card\"), shadow = document.getElementById(\"tt-shadow\");\nvar thickness = num(vars.thickness, 22, 4, 80), turns = num(vars.turns, 1, 0.25, 4), tilt = num(vars.tilt, 8, -30, 30), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0, 4);\nvar C = { background: col(vars.background_color, \"#111111\"), front: col(vars.front_color, \"#E5322D\"), back: col(vars.back_color, \"#F2F2F2\"), edge: col(vars.edge_color, \"#A3201C\"), mark: col(vars.mark_color, \"#FFFFFF\"), shadow: col(vars.shadow_color, \"#000000\") };\nvar W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\nvar unit = H / 720, cardH = H * 0.46, cardW = cardH * 1.58;\n// Keep the card inside narrow frames.\nif (cardW > W * 0.8) { cardW = W * 0.8; cardH = cardW / 1.58; }\nvar depth = thickness * unit, radius = Math.min(cardH * 0.06, depth * 1.2);\nvar floorY = H / 2 + cardH / 2 + H * 0.075;\nroot.style.setProperty(\"--background\", C.background); root.style.setProperty(\"--front\", C.front); root.style.setProperty(\"--back\", C.back); root.style.setProperty(\"--edge\", C.edge); root.style.setProperty(\"--mark\", C.mark); root.style.setProperty(\"--shadow\", C.shadow);\nroot.style.setProperty(\"--floor\", (floorY / H) * 100 + \"%\");\npersp.style.perspective = H * 2.4 + \"px\";\ncard.style.width = cardW + \"px\"; card.style.height = cardH + \"px\";\nfunction slab(w, h) {\n  var s = document.createElement(\"div\"); s.className = \"tt-slab\";\n  s.style.left = (cardW - w) / 2 + \"px\"; s.style.top = (cardH - h) / 2 + \"px\"; s.style.width = w + \"px\"; s.style.height = h + \"px\";\n  card.appendChild(s); return s;\n}\nvar sR = slab(depth, cardH - radius * 2), sL = slab(depth, cardH - radius * 2), sT = slab(cardW - radius * 2, depth), sB = slab(cardW - radius * 2, depth);\nsR.style.transform = \"rotateY(90deg) translateZ(\" + cardW / 2 + \"px)\";\nsL.style.transform = \"rotateY(-90deg) translateZ(\" + cardW / 2 + \"px)\";\nsT.style.transform = \"rotateX(90deg) translateZ(\" + cardH / 2 + \"px)\"; sT.style.filter = \"brightness(1.1)\";\nsB.style.transform = \"rotateX(-90deg) translateZ(\" + cardH / 2 + \"px)\"; sB.style.filter = \"brightness(0.6)\";\nfunction face(inner, transform) {\n  var f = document.createElement(\"div\"); f.className = \"tt-face\";\n  f.style.borderRadius = radius + \"px\"; f.style.transform = transform; f.style.fontSize = cardH / 30 + \"px\";\n  f.innerHTML = '<div class=\"tt-content\">' + inner + '</div><div class=\"tt-sheen\"></div><div class=\"tt-dark\"></div>';\n  card.appendChild(f);\n  return { sheen: f.querySelector(\".tt-sheen\"), dark: f.querySelector(\".tt-dark\") };\n}\nvar fr = face('<div class=\"tt-front\"><div class=\"tt-ring\"></div><div class=\"tt-lines\"><div class=\"tt-line\" style=\"width:62%\"></div><div class=\"tt-line\" style=\"width:38%;opacity:.55\"></div></div></div>', \"translateZ(\" + depth / 2 + \"px)\");\nvar bk = face('<div class=\"tt-backf\"><div class=\"tt-strip\"></div><div class=\"tt-chip\"></div></div>', \"rotateY(180deg) translateZ(\" + depth / 2 + \"px)\");\nshadow.style.top = floorY - H * 0.025 + \"px\"; shadow.style.height = H * 0.05 + \"px\"; shadow.style.filter = \"blur(\" + H * 0.018 + \"px)\";\nvar START = 6, END = 64, spinEase = bez(0.55, 0, 0.25, 1);\nfunction light(nx, nz) { return 0.55 + 0.45 * Math.max(0, nz * 0.85 - nx * 0.5); }\nfunction draw(frame) {\n  var t = frame * speed;\n  var angle = interp(t, [START, END], [0, 1], spinEase) * 360 * turns, rad = (angle * Math.PI) / 180;\n  var cos = Math.cos(rad), sin = Math.sin(rad);\n  var sheen = 50 + sin * 120;\n  card.style.transform = \"rotateX(\" + -tilt + \"deg) rotateY(\" + angle + \"deg)\";\n  sR.style.filter = \"brightness(\" + light(cos, -sin) + \")\";\n  sL.style.filter = \"brightness(\" + light(-cos, sin) + \")\";\n  [[fr, light(sin, cos)], [bk, light(-sin, -cos)]].forEach(function (f) {\n    f[0].sheen.style.background = \"linear-gradient(105deg, rgba(255,255,255,0) \" + (sheen - 22) + \"%, rgba(255,255,255,0.22) \" + sheen + \"%, rgba(255,255,255,0) \" + (sheen + 22) + \"%)\";\n    f[0].dark.style.opacity = 1 - f[1];\n  });\n  var footprint = Math.abs(cos) * cardW + Math.abs(sin) * depth, shadowW = Math.max(footprint, depth * 3);\n  shadow.style.left = W / 2 - shadowW / 2 + \"px\"; shadow.style.width = shadowW + \"px\";\n  shadow.style.opacity = 0.45 + 0.35 * Math.abs(cos);\n}\nfinish(drive(draw, TOTAL));\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
